<lint-cmd>                    # e.g. ruff check . / eslint .
<build-cmd>                   # e.g. npm run build / cargo build --release
```

## Code conventions

These are the conventions claude-leverage documents and enforces (see the
`AGENTS.md` of the claude-leverage repo for the full rationale).

### AIDEV-* anchor comments

Three grep-able prefixes for load-bearing facts in code:

- `AIDEV-NOTE:` — why this constraint exists / non-obvious invariant
- `AIDEV-TODO:` — known follow-up with enough context to resume
- `AIDEV-QUESTION:` — genuine unknown for the next person (or agent)

Rules: ≤120 chars per line, all-caps prefix. **Before editing a module, run
`grep -rn 'AIDEV-' <module>` first.** Do not silently remove anchors —
removing one requires an explicit decision in the commit / PR message.

The `ai-first-nudge` PostToolUse hook from claude-leverage prints a
non-blocking suggestion when ≥50 net-new LOC ship in a single file without
any anchor.

### Structured JSON-lines logging

When code emits logs that an agent will later read:

```json
{"ts":"2026-01-01T12:00:00.000Z","level":"info","trace_id":"a1b2","span_id":"4d5e","service":"<svc>","event":"<snake_case>","attrs":{"<key>":"<value>"}}
```

Required fields: `ts`, `level`, `trace_id`, `span_id`, `service`, `event`,
`attrs`. **Do not interpolate values into messages**: put `user_id` in
`attrs.user_id`, not in the `message` string.

### Per-directory AGENTS.md

For modules with non-obvious public surface or gotchas, drop an `AGENTS.md`
at the module root with: what lives here, public surface, gotchas, test
command. Codex merges nested AGENTS.md from git root down to cwd
automatically.

### Module organization

- Co-locate tests with code (`foo.py` next to `foo_test.py`) where the
  language/framework supports it.
- One concept per module, thin entrypoint exporting the public surface.
- Predictable file layout, documented above in "Repo layout".

## Security

<!-- Project-specific guardrails. Always-on hooks from claude-leverage cover
     secrets in staged diffs and dangerous git operations independently. -->

- Never commit secrets, including in test fixtures. Use placeholder
  strings the `block-secrets-precommit` hook recognizes as safe (or add
  the `claude-leverage-allow-secret` marker comment per line if you must).
- Run `/security-review` before committing changes in:
  `<list sensitive paths: auth/, crypto/, routes/, payment/, templates/, …>`.

